+# A1 candidate implementation: first review snapshot
+
+Branch: dev/video-trajectory-blind-validation-v1; base e6050c8.
+No model/GPU/Colab run, push, merge or commit was performed.
+
+The original lattice function and protocol/config are retained. The new pure
+FP64 solver has projected-gradient updates, a full-simplex Frank-Wolfe gap
+certificate with a rounding cushion, and fail-closed numerical failure.
+The existing real feedback loop now accepts an explicit solver and independent
+saved point; its historical default stays the lattice. The new candidate
+wrapper selects the continuous solver and separately binds its protocol/config.
+Failures cannot become ZERO_OPTIMUM or advance a sequential control chain.
+
+The fixed six-point entrypoint verifies all original saved artifact hashes,
+restores complete native scheduler history, recomputes the original basis and
+requires old raw/masked full-byte hashes, then reuses the real feedback loop.
+Each saved T46/47/48 point has its own original state/history and spent=0.
+Sequential continuation through the wrapper remains the original loop, which
+recomputes q/J after committing each accepted first-step history.
+
+CPU validation:
+
+- Python: /home/richar/projects/CEG-WM/alive/CEG-WM/.venv/bin/python.
+- numpy 2.5.2, pytest 9.1.1, torch 2.5.1+cpu, diffusers 0.39.0.
+- `python -m pytest tests/test_rgb_dct_continuous_solver.py tests/test_rgb_dct_structured_feedback.py -q`: 18 passed in 9.58s.
+- Includes analytic fine-scale optimum/lattice-zero counterexample, exact zero,
+  unavailable directions, budget boundary, tiny nonzero, exhausted iteration,
+  nonfinite arithmetic, real-loop fail-stop, accepted sequential history/q
+  refresh, independent single-point nonadvancement and six-row failure retention.
+- Existing native UniPC CPU checks use a fake Transformer. They do not validate
+  the real model or the Colab diffusers 0.40.0 runtime numerics.
+- `git diff --check`: passed.
+
+Saved proxy replay: `python -m scripts.replay_video_trajectory_surrogates`
+with the original audit `result.json` and `offline_review.json`, output
+`saved_surrogate_replay.json`: 6/6 certified, 0 failure. Gap bounds range from
+6.7174e-18 to 1.0058e-16; maximum objective difference from prior independently
+computed continuous solutions is 1.6941e-21. All six original grid solutions
+remain zero. This is saved-proxy CPU evidence only, with no real candidate tail,
+MP4, blind detector or payload result.
+
+The original audit input directory is
+`/home/richar/projects/Video-WM/diagnostics/method-mechanism-audit-20260928/structured_feedback_review`.
+Original files were read without modification. A4 independently reports that
+all 26 original Drive .pt artifacts were read and SHA256 matched this session.
+The new preflight will repeat byte verification immediately before the real run.
+
+Notebook: `notebooks/video_trajectory_blind_validation_v1_colab.ipynb`.
